  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 7e787bb2f794a6a4695134e4583867ae, type: 3}
  m_Name: Ophilia Jones Portrait encounter
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::Character
  charName: Eternity
  characterSprite: {fileID: 8013740796401983728, guid: bc45d0c45810e4f4c8ec60be231b7e55, type: 3}
  lines:
  - "This portrait\u2026 it\u2019s my father."
  - "He was a very strict man. The kind who believed emotions were something to be
    corrected, not spoken about. He never really heard my cries\u2026 only what he
    expected them to become."
  - He always gave me a cold shoulder, as if warmth might distract me from becoming
    what he wanted.
  - "But my last memory of him\u2026 it was different."
  - "I remember him sitting alone in his study, the same room I always saw him in\u2026
    but he wasn\u2019t the same. He looked tired. Not in body, but in something deeper.
    Like something in him had finally cracked."
  - "I think\u2026 he was sad that I was sad."
  - "And I didn\u2019t know what to do with that."
  - I remember wanting to say something to him. Something simple. Something that
    would fix it. But the words never came out properly.
  - "Oh\u2026 Father."
  - I miss you dearly.
  - "I wonder if you\u2019re here somewhere too."
